cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Frankl's conjecture beyond cyclic symmetry: a SAT-certified theorem for all transitive groups on 14 points"
authors:
  - family-names: Albanese
    given-names: Simone
type: software
date-released: 2026-08-12
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21920980
abstract: >-
  Computer-assisted proof that no non-trivial union-closed family invariant
  under any transitive permutation group on 14 points violates Frankl's
  union-closed sets conjecture. A census of the 63 transitive groups of degree
  14 and a certified minimality reduction collapse the problem to five SAT
  instances (plus the previously certified cyclic case), each decided by two
  independent exact methods (OR-Tools CP-SAT and CaDiCaL) with DRAT
  certificates verified by drat-trim. The campaign was executed autonomously
  by an AI agent loop built on Anthropic's Claude Code (model Claude Fable 5)
  under human supervision.
